        <li><strong>Standard Time Period (November to March):</strong> Eastern U.S. locations operate on <strong>EST (UTC-5)</strong>. The difference from SAST is <strong>7 hours</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Daylight Saving Period (March to November):</strong> Eastern U.S. locations operate on <strong>EDT (UTC-4)</strong>. The difference from SAST becomes <strong>6 hours</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For instance, when it is 15:00 SAST in Johannesburg:
      </p>
      <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; margin: 1rem 0;">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem;"><strong>In Winter (EST, UTC-5):</strong> 15:00 SAST − 7 hours = <strong>08:00 AM EST</strong></p>
        <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>In Summer (EDT, UTC-4):</strong> 15:00 SAST − 6 hours = <strong>09:00 AM EDT</strong></p>
      </div>
    </section>

