      <p>
        Because SAST is 7 hours ahead of EST, early morning hours in South Africa land on the <strong>previous calendar day</strong> in Eastern Standard Time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any SAST time occurring between 00:00 (midnight) and 06:59 AM corresponds to evening hours between 17:00 (5:00 PM) and 23:59 (11:59 PM) on the <em>preceding calendar day</em> in North America.
      </p>

      <h3>Date Rollover Window</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li><strong>00:00 SAST:</strong> 17:00 EST on the <strong>Previous Calendar Day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>03:00 SAST:</strong> 20:00 EST on the <strong>Previous Calendar Day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>06:00 SAST:</strong> 23:00 EST on the <strong>Previous Calendar Day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>07:00 SAST:</strong> 00:00 EST on the <strong>SAME Calendar Day</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For example, a scheduled software migration taking place at 02:00 AM SAST on Tuesday, October 15 occurs at 7:00 PM EST on Monday, October 14.
      </p>
    </section>

